From: sullivan@blaze.cs.jhu.edu (Gregory Sullivan)
Date: Mon, 21 Nov 94 00:05:04 EST
Subject: [#94-11-287] META: Stopping unsubscribe messages

Periodically messages from individuals who wish to unsubscribe from the list
are posted to everyone.  It is a minor annoyance which may be partially
avoided.  What do you think of the following idea?  Messages with the word
``unsubscribe'' are intercepted and not posted to the list. (The match is
insensitive to capitalization.) Instead a message of the following type is
sent back to the original sender.

Begin sample message:

You have attempted to send a message to all members of the extropian
electronic mailing list which contains the word ``unsubscribe''.  Your
message was intercepted and was not sent to the list readers. If you wish to
unsubscribe from this list then please send your message requesting this to
extropians-request@extropy.org.  We are interested in monitoring and
improving the quality of the extropians list and therefore we would also
appreciate the voluntary inclusion of a short statement indicating why you
wish to unsubscribe. Thank you.

If you really do not wish to unsubscribe but your message just happens to
contain the word ``unsubscribe'' then it is possible to override this
interception mechanism. Include the classic magic word ``xyzzy'' in the body
of your message and it will be posted to all members of the list.

     Thanks, Extropian list management

End sample message.

This mechanism could be extended to search for close matches to other words
and phrases such as:  ``remove me from ... list '' where the ellipses
matches zero, one or two arbitrary words. 
This would match phrases such as:
    remove me from this list
    remove me from the extropian list

Other more elaborate matching ideas are possible but the payoff no doubt
diminishes.      Gregory Sullivan

